    <h1>SITETRACK MASTER TERMS OF SERVICE (B2B SaaS)</h1>
    <p><strong>Last Updated:</strong> [Insert Date]</p>

    <p>This Master Terms of Service Agreement (the "Agreement") is entered into by and between [Insert Company Name] ABN [Insert ABN] (hereinafter referred to as "SiteTrack", "we", "us", or "our") and the business entity registering for the SiteTrack platform (hereinafter referred to as the "Customer", "you", or "your").</p>
    
    <p>By registering for an account, accessing, or using the SiteTrack software platform (the "Service"), you acknowledge that you have read, understood, and agree to be bound by this Agreement. If you do not agree to these terms, you must not access or use the Service.</p>

    <h2>1. DEFINITIONS</h2>
    <ol>
        <li><span class="clause">"Authorised User"</span> means any employee, contractor, or agent of the Customer who has been granted access credentials to the Service by the Customer.</li>
        <li><span class="clause">"Customer Data"</span> means all information, data, and materials entered into the Service by the Customer or its Authorised Users.</li>
        <li><span class="clause">"Service"</span> means the SiteTrack web applications, mobile applications, APIs, and associated cloud infrastructure.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>2. PROVISION OF THE SERVICE & NATURE OF SOFTWARE</h2>
    <ol>
        <li><span class="clause">License Grant:</span> Subject to the terms of this Agreement and payment of all applicable fees, SiteTrack grants the Customer a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, and revocable license to access and use the Service strictly for its internal business operations.</li>
        <li><span class="clause">Not a Certifying Authority:</span> The Customer expressly acknowledges and agrees that SiteTrack provides a digital software tool for data management. SiteTrack is <strong>NOT</strong> an engineering firm, fire safety certifying authority, or compliance regulatory body. SiteTrack does not verify the physical reality, accuracy, or legal compliance of any Customer Data.</li>
        <li><span class="clause">AS 1851-2012 Compliance:</span> The Customer holds sole, absolute, and unconditional responsibility for ensuring that all fire safety inspections, maintenance, reporting, and physical works comply with Australian Standard 1851-2012 and any other applicable state or federal legislation. SiteTrack shall bear zero responsibility for any failure of fire protection systems, property damage, injury, death, or regulatory non-compliance resulting from the Customer's operations.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>3. CUSTOMER OBLIGATIONS</h2>
    <ol>
        <li><span class="clause">Account Security:</span> The Customer is entirely responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of its login credentials. The Customer agrees to immediately notify SiteTrack of any unauthorized use of its accounts.</li>
        <li><span class="clause">Authorised Users:</span> The Customer guarantees that all Authorised Users are at least eighteen (18) years of age and hold the necessary valid professional licenses (e.g., FPAS accreditation) required by law to perform their duties.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>4. DATA OWNERSHIP AND PRIVACY</h2>
    <ol>
        <li><span class="clause">Ownership:</span> The Customer retains all rights, title, and interest in and to the Customer Data.</li>
        <li><span class="clause">License to Host:</span> The Customer grants SiteTrack a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive license to host, copy, transmit, and display Customer Data solely as necessary for SiteTrack to provide the Service.</li>
        <li><span class="clause">Privacy Act 1988 Compliance:</span> SiteTrack will process personal information in accordance with its Privacy Policy and the Australian Privacy Principles. The Customer consents to the potential transfer and processing of Customer Data on servers located outside of Australia (including the United States).</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>5. FEES AND PAYMENT</h2>
    <ol>
        <li><span class="clause">Subscription Fees:</span> The Customer agrees to pay all fees associated with their chosen subscription plan. All fees are non-refundable unless otherwise required by Australian Consumer Law.</li>
        <li><span class="clause">Suspension for Non-Payment:</span> SiteTrack reserves the right to immediately suspend the Customer's access to the Service if any payment is overdue.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>6. DISCLAIMER OF WARRANTIES</h2>
    <p class="all-caps">To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, the Service is provided strictly on an "AS IS" and "AS AVAILABLE" basis. SiteTrack expressly disclaims all warranties of any kind, whether express, implied, statutory, or otherwise, including but not limited to the implied warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement. SiteTrack does not warrant that the Service will be uninterrupted, error-free, entirely secure, or that it will meet the Customer's specific regulatory requirements.</p>

    <h2>7. INDEMNIFICATION</h2>
    <p>The Customer agrees to fully indemnify, defend, and hold harmless SiteTrack, its directors, officers, employees, and agents from and against any and all claims, liabilities, damages, losses, regulatory fines, and legal costs (on a full indemnity basis) arising out of or in connection with:</p>
    <ol>
        <li>The Customer's or Authorised Users' use of the Service;</li>
        <li>Any property damage, personal injury, or death resulting from the failure of fire safety equipment inspected or maintained by the Customer;</li>
        <li>Any breach of AS 1851-2012 or other applicable laws by the Customer; or</li>
        <li>Any falsified, inaccurate, or incomplete data entered into the platform by the Customer.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>8. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY</h2>
    <p class="all-caps">In no event shall SiteTrack be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, punitive, or exemplary damages, including but not limited to loss of profits, loss of revenue, business interruption, loss of data, or property damage, even if SiteTrack has been advised of the possibility of such damages.</p>
    <p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, SiteTrack’s total cumulative liability for any direct damages arising out of or relating to this Agreement (whether in contract, tort including negligence, or otherwise) shall be strictly limited to the total amount of subscription fees actually paid by the Customer to SiteTrack in the one (1) month immediately preceding the event giving rise to the claim.</p>

    <h2>9. TERM AND TERMINATION</h2>
    <ol>
        <li><span class="clause">Term:</span> This Agreement commences on the date of account registration and continues until terminated by either party.</li>
        <li><span class="clause">Termination for Convenience:</span> Either party may terminate this Agreement by providing thirty (30) days written notice.</li>
        <li><span class="clause">Termination for Cause:</span> SiteTrack may terminate this Agreement immediately and without notice if the Customer materially breaches any provision of this Agreement, including the Acceptable Use Policy.</li>
        <li><span class="clause">Data Export:</span> Upon termination, the Customer will have a period of thirty (30) days to export their Customer Data, after which SiteTrack may permanently delete all associated data without liability.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>10. GENERAL PROVISIONS</h2>
    <ol>
        <li><span class="clause">Governing Law:</span> This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of [Insert State, e.g., Victoria/New South Wales], Australia. The parties submit to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of that State.</li>
        <li><span class="clause">Force Majeure:</span> SiteTrack shall not be liable for any failure or delay in performance due to circumstances beyond its reasonable control, including acts of God, internet outages, cyber-attacks, or governmental actions.</li>
        <li><span class="clause">Severability:</span> If any provision of this Agreement is held to be invalid or unenforceable, the remaining provisions shall continue in full force and effect.</li>
    </ol>

